            val flightTime = (distanceToFisher.pow(0.2) * 20 * 0.6).coerceAtLeast(0.01)

            fish.noAITicks = 20
            fish.launch(ev.player.location, flightTime)
        }
    }
}
```

Admittedly, some of these handlers can get quite messy and this is one of the areas of MidnightSky that I'd like to improve on during one of my future refactoring sessions.

### 7.2 Alliances

**Overview**  
Alliances give players a way to make organized groups. An alliance is a group of up to 15 players that usually all play on a single island. The alliance must have one ``Leader`` and everyone else can have one of a few different roles like Officer or even just Member.

Each server must keep a cached copy of the alliance of each player currently on that server, it is uncached when there are no remaining players of that alliance on that server. The copies must be kept because there are lots of game mechanics that rely on being able to query alliance information without block or delay. However, the copies are read-only and any changes must be made via the Alliance Service, which has the following outline functions:

```kotlin
